course: dictionary
lesson: 9596
title: One word, many stretches
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word stretch has several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. To stretch can mean to make something longer or wider by pulling it, or to push your arms, legs or body out as far as they go.
explain: Stretch can also mean to spread over a distance or a length of time. «The beach stretches for miles.» Nothing is being pulled here. The beach simply reaches a long way.
explain: Use context to choose. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense. «A cobra lifts the front of its body and spreads long ribs in its neck to stretch the skin into a hood» means the skin is pulled wider, so the pulling meaning fits.
explain: Stretch also works as a noun: a stretch is a long piece of land, water, road or time. «We walked a long stretch of road before lunch» tells you the road was long, and «at a stretch» means without stopping.
fact: Stretch can be a verb (to stretch) or a noun (a stretch).
fact: «Stretch» means to make something longer or wider by pulling it, or to spread over a distance or time.
fact: «A stretch» means a long piece of land, water, road or time.
fact: Elastic materials, like rubber bands, stretch and spring back.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The beach stretches for miles.» What does stretches mean here? | *Spreads over a long distance | Pushes out arms and legs | Pulls something tighter | Snaps in two
exercise: In science, rubber bands stretch and spring back. What does stretch mean here? | To freeze completely still | *To pull something to make it longer | To shout loudly
exercise: «We walked a long stretch of road before lunch.» What is a stretch in this sentence? | *A long piece of road | A quick jump | A kind of shoe | A loud noise
test: «Sam stretched out his arms and yawned.» What does stretched mean? | Cried loudly | Shrank small | Hid under the covers | *Pushed his arms out as far as they go
test: «He wanted to stretch his legs after the long car ride.» What does stretch his legs mean? | Sit still for hours | Pull his legs off | Fall asleep in the car | *Get up and move about
exam: «A drinks can starts as a flat disc of aluminium and is stretched tall.» Which meaning of stretched fits best? | Spread over miles | *Made longer by pulling | To yawn and rest | A long piece of road
